\f1\fs22 Chanta had spent three hours orchestrating the perfect evening. The view from his penthouse was set to \'93Golden Hour Aurora Australis\'94. Even nature couldn\'92t compete with his wealth anymore. The fourteen-course meal prepared by Executive Chef Rosalind Carpenter sat under cloches, each dish more intricately expensive than the last. None of the courses involved burgers or fries; despite Chanta\'92s pleas, the Executive Chef offered multiple alternative potato sides, and refused to serve burgers of any kind, unless they were \'93deconstructed\'94, which seemed to absurd to Chanta who did not want to construct his own burger while trying to impress his important guest. What did he pay a chef for, anyway?\
