\cf2 \'93So,\'94 he said, spreading his arms wide as Sarah entered, \'93what do you think? King of the world, baby.\'94\
Sarah took in the absurd luxury with a mixture of amusement and unease. Her eyes kept returning to Tony. He looked\'85 extraordinary. Not dressed-up extraordinary. Not \'93new money did a makeover\'94 extraordinary. Just wrong-well. His skin had an almost luminescent quality, his eyes bright and clear, his whole bearing radiating a vitality that didn\'92t match the life he\'92d been living.\
When had Tony become so devastatingly handsome?\
\'93It\'92s certainly... shiny.\'94\
\'93Shiny? This is the apex of civilisation!\'94 Chanta gestured grandly. \'93Voice-activated climate control, bidets that play \'91Evolve Me Tender\'92 or whatever you want.  I\'92ve got it all.\'94\
Fisher glided forward, offering Sarah a drink. \'93Champagne from the Napoleon cellar, madam? It predates even the Dark Ages.\'94\
\'93Just water, thanks.\'94\
Fisher poured for Chanta. \
\'93Since when do you have servants?\'94 Sarah asked.\
\'93They\'92re staff,\'94 Chanta corrected. \'93And they love working here. Right, Fisher?\'94\
\'93Indeed, sir. Though I must note that yesterday you referred to us as \'91Brylcreem security,\'92\'94 Fisher replied with artificial cheerfulness.\
\'93That was before I adjusted to my new station in life.\'94 Chanta swept an arm toward the table\'97twenty feet of crystal and linen set up like a diplomatic summit. \'93You know what else changed? Me. I\'92m ready now, Sarah. Ready for... us.\'94\
The absurdity of it\'97shouting across a runway of cutlery to have an intimate conversation\'97made Sarah laugh despite herself.\
Chanta took that laugh like a favourable market signal and began feeding her course after ridiculous course, narrating his own sophistication between bites.\
\'93And check this out,\'94 he said, standing up as if the apartment required live demonstration. \'93Chanta wants music. Sexy music.\'94\
Immediately, an orchestra of the Elvi\'92s most romantic ballads swelled through hidden speakers.\
\'93Chanta wants mood lighting.\'94\
The lights dimmed to a golden glow, somehow making his hair gleam despite its recent lack of grooming. The same glow caught his cheekbones, and for a moment Sarah had the disorienting sense that he\'92d been polished from the inside.\
\'93Chanta wants\'97\'94\
\'93Chanta wants to stop talking in third person?\'94 Sarah suggested.\
Chanta laughed, delighted, and for a few minutes it was easy. Too easy. His boyish enthusiasm mixed with his new confidence into something unexpectedly appealing, and Sarah found herself leaning into it, letting the evening carry her along despite the faint, nagging sense that she was being carried by something else.\
Eventually, after dinner, they abandoned the table for the living room\'97vast, soft, expensive. Chanta flopped down as if he belonged there by divine right.\
\'93You know,\'94 Sarah said, \'93I think I preferred you as Mr. Fairy Boxers.\'94\
Chanta\'92s grin was pure delight. \'93You remember those?\'94\
\'93Hard to forget. You were so proud of them, even when you were sleeping in refrigerators.\'94\
\'93Now I could buy a thousand pairs. Want to see my collection?\'94\
\'93Please tell me you didn\'92t actually\'97\'94\
\'93Framed. In the master suite. Very tasteful.\'94\
This made her laugh again, and suddenly they were closer than they\'92d been in months. Tony caught her hand; his skin was warm and vibrant against hers, his thumb tracing her knuckles with an ease that made her forget to think.\
\'93Sarah...\'94 he began, but she was already leaning toward him.\
The kiss started tentatively but deepened as months of separation dissolved. When Chanta\'92s hand moved to her waist, she didn\'92t pull away. Instead, she let herself be drawn closer.\
\'93We shouldn\'92t,\'94 she murmured against his lips.\
\'93Probably not,\'94 he agreed, continuing the kiss.\
They moved to the plush sofa, Chanta\'92s confidence making the transition smooth. His hands were sure as they began removing her jacket. Sarah responded, matching his intensity as they unbuttoned both clothing and inhibitions, even as something inside her kept trying to sit up and clear its throat.\
Chanta instinctively put his hand on Sarah\'92s belly, over Little Clinton, then immediately recoiled, his mind overtaken by strange visions and thoughts.\
\'93What\'92s the matter?\'94 Sarah asked as Chanta sat back for her.\
No amount of knitting his eyebrows together was making an answer any clearer. \'93I don\'92t know\'85 I saw and old boat, called 
